39,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The data suggests that external logistics are unreliable. Scanning contractors have unstable delivery windows, and road closures affect our access, though not the community halls themselves. We must avoid services that rely on fragile schedules.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh wow, it's even worse than I thought! People in the outer wards have to travel an hour now, but they used to come in huge numbers to the outreach stops. We really need to reach them!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,George,,"The financial records are concerning. Our vehicle costs are overrunning, and the county grants only cover session fees for a year. We must be careful not to commit to something that drains our operating budget.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,May,,"It's exactly as I feared. We tried digitisation years ago and it was a mess, yet the partner-run groups are still thriving. We should look for models that are self-sustaining rather than top-down projects.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found out that we have some skilled volunteers, but we don't have any staff trained to supervise outside facilitators. Also, the person who certified our power tools has retired. I'm worried about who will manage things.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, if vehicle costs are already overrunning, a mobile service might be a liability. @May, your finding about the partner-run groups suggests that community-led models are the most stable. We need a low-dependency option.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"But we can't just ignore the people who can't reach us! If the outer wards are struggling and they loved the outreach stops, we have to find a way to bring the library to them.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I understand your passion, but we cannot ignore the ledger. If the vehicle line is already overrunning by a third, adding more mileage is a recipe for a budget crisis by the second year.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, you're right about the money, but @Yumi is right about the need. If we want stability, we should look at those partner-run groups I found. They've lasted six years without us hovering.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""George"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried that if we start something new, we won't have anyone to supervise it. We have volunteers, but no staff trained for facilitators, and our tool certification has lapsed. We shouldn't start something we can't safely manage.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, your point about supervision is critical. If we lack the internal capacity to manage facilitators or certify tools, we risk failure. We need a proposal that leverages existing community strengths without creating new staff burdens.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"But if we don't do something, those people are just left behind! Is there any way to use those partner groups @May mentioned to help the outer wards without needing a big budget or new staff?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, that is a sensible direction. If we can utilize community partners, we might avoid the funding trap where the grant expires and the operating budget collapses. We must find a balance between access and fiscal reality.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,May,,"Exactly. We need to stop pretending every new idea is a fresh start. If we lean into the partner-led model that's already proven to survive, we solve the budget and supervision issues simultaneously.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think that sounds safer. If the community already knows how to run things, maybe our staff won't be so overwhelmed. I just don't want us to promise something we can't actually support.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We have established that high-cost vehicle operations, unreliable contractors, and lack of internal supervision are our primary risks. A model based on community partnerships seems the most resilient and sustainable path forward. I am ready for the candidates.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I agree! As long as we can still help the people in the outer wards who are cut off, I'm on board with a community-led approach. I can't wait to see the options!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,George,,I agree. We must prioritize a service that is fiscally sustainable and does not rely on a temporary grant to survive its second year. Let us see which candidates fit these criteria.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm glad we're finally on the same page. Let's see if any of these candidates actually reflect the lessons of the past, or if we're just about to repeat the same mistakes.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I hope the candidates have a plan for who will actually do the work. I'll support whatever is safest for the staff and the community. I'm ready to see them.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
